From 86ca187afb30704201df49a297832fb3a05f6223 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: horizon-prism <horizon-prism@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:13:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat: launch Horizon instances with horizon-client (M3)

Horizon instances now run the real client instead of failing at the launch
placeholder:

- HorizonLaunchStep builds the session from AuthSession (name, dashless
  uuid, access_token, user_type) and writes it to horizon-client's stdin
  via --session-stdin, so tokens never appear in argv or logs;
- it passes --resources, --game-dir, --home, window size and quick-play,
  probes --launch-api to check the pinned launch API and to read
  crash_report_line, and maps exit codes 0/1/2/101 to clear messages;
- HorizonInstance resolves horizon-client from horizon.json clientPath,
  the pinned clientVersion, any installed version, or PATH;
- HorizonNotPrepared now only fails when the resources are missing and
  otherwise lets the launch step run.

Tested with the real nightly 2026-11-13 client: 98 s prepare, --frames 2,
exit 0, first frame rendered, smoke report without error.

Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
